drills.prompt:
Find the range and the interquartile range of these 10 values (use the
median-of-halves method for quartiles):

{d1}, {d2}, {d3}, {d4}, {d5}, {d6}, {d7}, {d8}, {d9}, {d10}

Here are 11 sorted values:

{a1}, {a2}, {a3}, {a4}, {a5}, {a6}, {a7}, {a8}, {a9}, {a10}, {a11}

Find $Q_1$, the median and $Q_3$.

Packages have mean weight {mu} kg and standard deviation {sig} kg. A van carries {nn}
randomly selected packages and is rated for {cap} kg. What is the probability the total
weight exceeds the rating? Give 4 decimals.

drills.solution:
df $= {dfree}$, $t^* \approx {ts:dp3}$. $SE = {sx}/\sqrt{{nn}} \approx {se:num4}$;
$ME = {ts:dp3} \times {se:num4} \approx {me:num4}$. Interval: ${xbar} \pm {me:num4}$, from
**{lo:num2}** to **{hi:num2}**.

drills.prompt:
In a randomized experiment, {x1} of {n1} patients improved on treatment 1 and {x2} of {n2}
improved on treatment 2. Construct a {lev} confidence interval for $p_1 - p_2$ (endpoints
to 4 decimals).

drills.solution:
$\hat{p}_1 = {p1:num4}$, $\hat{p}_2 = {p2:num4}$, difference ${diff:num4}$.
$SE = \sqrt{\hat{p}_1(1-\hat{p}_1)/n_1 + \hat{p}_2(1-\hat{p}_2)/n_2} \approx {se:num4}$;
$ME = {lev:num4}({se:num4}) \approx {me:num4}$. Interval: **{lo:num4}** to **{hi:num4}**.

drills.prompt:
A manufacturer claims {p0} of its customers are repeat buyers. In a random sample of {nn}
customers, {xx} are repeat buyers. Test $H_0: p = {p0}$ against $H_a: p \ne {p0}$. Find the
z statistic (2 decimals) and the p-value (4 decimals).

drills.solution:
$\hat{p}_1 = {p1:num4}$, $\hat{p}_2 = {p2:num4}$. Pooled $\hat{p}_c = \dfrac{{xt}}{{nt}} =$ **{pc:num4}**.
$SE = \sqrt{\hat{p}_c(1-\hat{p}_c)(1/{n1} + 1/{n2})} \approx {se:num4}$;
$z = ({p1:num4} - {p2:num4})/{se:num4} \approx$ **{zz:num2}**; p-value $\approx$ **{pv:num4}**.
